                    "sw_access": "rw",
                    "se_onread": null,
                    "se_onwrite": null,
                    "desc": "Write 1 to start a hash. Self clearing. Writing this while a\nhash is already running restarts it from the beginning with the\ncurrently programmed configuration. Configuration is sampled at start,\nso changing CONFIG/PREPEND/FLASH_ADDR/LENGTH mid-hash has no effect on\nthe run in flight."
                },
                {
                    "type": "field",
                    "inst_name": "abort",
                    "lsb": 1,
                    "msb": 1,
                    "reset": 0,
                    "sw_access": "rw",
                    "se_onread": null,
                    "se_onwrite": null,
                    "desc": "Write 1 to abort a hash in flight. Self clearing. The engine\nreturns to idle, clears busy and sets STATUS.aborted. Any digest from\na previous run is discarded."
                }
            ]
        },
